## Why This Is Asked

This question tests a real-world KCNA pattern: dynamic routing controlled by a side-input, stateful enrichment with TTL, and delivery guarantees in the presence of config changes.

## Key Concepts

- State stores and TTL caches
- Side-input config streams
- Per-message offsets and at-least-once delivery
- ID-based deduplication across routing versions

## Code Example

```javascript
class RouterSink {
  constructor() {
    this.cache = new TTLCache({ ttl: 5 * 60 * 1000 }); // 5 minutes
  }

  onMessage(ctx, event) {
    const cached = this.cache.get(event.type);
    const route = cached?.route || 'default';

    emit({
      id: event.id,
      type: event.type,
      payload: event.payload,
      route,
      ts: event.ts
    });
  }

  onConfigUpdate(ctx, routingConfig) {
    for (const rule of routingConfig.rules) {
      this.cache.set(rule.eventType, { 
        route: rule.route, 
        version: routingConfig.version 
      });
    }
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests advanced fairness and isolation in a multi-tenant KCNA cluster; demonstrates practical reliability under bursty traffic.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant rate limiting (token bucket, leaky bucket)
- Global throughput vs. per-tenant isolation
- Distributed state store for buckets (Redis, etc.)
- Backpressure mechanisms and producer signaling
- Canary strategy and measurable success criteria

## Code Example

```javascript
// simplified token bucket sketch
class TokenBucket {
  constructor(rate, capacity) {
    this.rate = rate;
    this.capacity = capacity;
    this.tokens = capacity;
    this.lastRefill = Date.now();
  }

  allow(n = 1) {
    this.refill();
    if (this.tokens >= n) {
      this.tokens -= n;
      return true;
    }
    return false;
  }

  refill() {
    const now = Date.now();
    const elapsed = (now - this.lastRefill) / 1000;
    this.tokens = Math.min(this.capacity, this.tokens + elapsed * this.rate);
    this.lastRefill = now;
  }
}

// Global limiter wrapping per-tenant buckets
class TenantRateController {
  constructor(tenants, globalRate) {
    this.buckets = new Map();
    this.globalLimiter = new TokenBucket(globalRate, globalRate * 2);
    for (const [id, quota] of tenants) {
      this.buckets.set(id, new TokenBucket(quota.rate, quota.burst));
    }
  }

  tryProcess(tenantId, n = 1) {
    const bucket = this.buckets.get(tenantId);
    if (!bucket || !bucket.allow(n)) return false;
    if (!this.globalLimiter.allow(n)) {
      bucket.tokens += n; // rollback tenant token
      return false;
    }
    return true;
  }
}
```

