// Pseudo: set TTL for a tenant-topic
async function setTTL(tenantId, topic, ttlMs) {
  // persist TTL in config store per tenant-topic
  await configStore.set(`/tenants/${tenantId}/topics/${topic}/ttl`, ttlMs);
}

// Pseudo: purge loop (simplified)
function purgeOldMessages(tenantId, topic) {
  const ttlMs = configStore.get(`/tenants/${tenantId}/topics/${topic}/ttl`);
  const cutoff = Date.now() - ttlMs;
  for (const msg of storage.scan(tenantId, topic)) {
    if (msg.timestamp < cutoff) {
      storage.delete(msg.id);
      // emit tombstone to preserve replay semantics
      storage.appendTombstone({ tenantId, topic, id: msg.id });
    }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle TTL changes mid-flight without losing data consistency?
- How do you verify no live consumers are affected during purge windows?

## Why This Question Is Asked

This question evaluates real-world stateful Kafka Streams processing with a TTL-backed side-input, focusing on correctness under cache miss, update, and eviction scenarios, as well as robust testing strategies. It also assesses the ability to design APIs and observability for per-user enrichment in a high-throughput pipeline.

## Key Concepts

- TTL-based caching and eviction semantics
- Side-input-driven cache updates
- Per-message offset guarantees and at-least-once delivery
- Idempotent emits and deduplication

## Code Example

```java
// Implementation sketch
class FraudScoringSink implements KafkaSink {
  private final LoadingCache<String, RiskProfile> cache;

  public FraudScoringSink() {
    this.cache = Caffeine.newBuilder()
      .expireAfterWrite(10, TimeUnit.MINUTES)
      .build(CacheLoader.from(this::fetchFromStore));
  }

  @StreamListener
  public void onTransaction(Transaction txn) {
    RiskProfile profile = cache.getIfPresent(txn.userId());
    if (profile == null) {
      profile = RiskProfile.unknown();
    }
    emit(txn.enrich(profile));
  }

  @StreamListener
  public void onFraudSignal(FraudSignal signal) {
    cache.put(signal.userId(), signal.toProfile());
  }
}
```

## Testing Strategy

```java
@Test
void cacheMissEmitsUnknownAndReEnrichesOnSignal() {
  store.onTransaction(tx("u1", 100));
  verify(emit).calledWith(risk="unknown");

  store.onFraudSignal(signal("u1", 0.9, "velocity"));
  verify(emit).calledWith(risk="high");
}

@Test
void ttlEvictionClearsStaleRiskData() {
  cache.put("u1", profile(0.8));
  clock.advance(11, MINUTES);
  cache.cleanUp();
  assertNull(cache.getIfPresent("u1"));
}
```

